308:The ETTm2-source rows add a complementary direction. ETTm2 transfers strongly to ETTh1 after fine-tuning, and it also transfers effectively to ETTh2 relative to target self-training. The ETTh2 H=96/H=192 rows illustrate an important distinction: fine-tuning remains much better than target self-training, but zero-shot is already even stronger, so additional target adaptation is not always necessary. This supports two separate transfer claims: zero-shot transfer measures direct deployability of the source representation, while fine-tuning measures whether source initialization improves target training relative to random initialization.
